---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/config';
---
<Base title={`about · ${site.title}`} current="about">
  <header style="padding: 48px 0 24px 0">
    <h1 class="display" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 76px)">about</h1>
  </header>
  <div class="prose" style="max-width: 720px">
    <p>I'm Trevor Burton-McCreadie, a bitter ex-musician turned software engineer who helps organisations build intelligent software systems that solve real business problems. With more than two decades of experience across the full software stack, from embedded devices and cloud infrastructure to backend platforms, frontend applications and AI, I have worked with a wide range of languages, frameworks and distributed architectures across industries including manufacturing, food technology, financial services and online gaming.</p>
    <p>Like everyone else right now I'm trying to work out how to make the best use of AI. Most of my time is spent building software for organisations with difficult problems to solve: figuring out where AI genuinely adds value, where conventional software engineering is still the better answer, and how the two can co-exist.</p>
    <p>thinkmorestupidless is the name the work has gone under since 2017. Everything here is public, and so are the brains: one small repository per family that holds the map, the pins, the decisions and the traps, written for people and agents alike. Most of the code on this account was written with an agent beside it, and the brains are how that stays on track.</p>
    <h2>how this site works</h2>
    <p>It is rendered from GitHub. The families, their repositories, their releases and when they were last touched are read at build time; the writing is markdown in the site's own repository. When a repository tags a release, the site redraws itself. The tool is <a href={`https://github.com/${site.owner}/${site.repo}`}>w3</a>, and it will render any account the same way.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
